+## Returning to the game
+
+The standalone page keeps **Return to game** beside its existing workshop actions, including before startup finishes and when theme loading fails. It is a normal relative link to `../../game/`, so an immutable release or local edition returns to its own game entry. It does not restore the former Workshop menu or its opener, start or resume a flight, or automatically Apply unsaved authoring choices. Use Apply explicitly to keep those choices before leaving.
+
+Back and Escape inside the catalog still close its dialog; they do not navigate away. The practice iframe retains its existing input and scoped Return to workshop bridge. The page's shared controller navigation can select Return to game after successful startup and once the dialog is closed; before startup completes or after it fails, the link remains an ordinary keyboard/pointer action.
+
+Maintenance prompt: “Hold then fail the real theme request and verify Return to game is still a usable same-edition link without running authoring handlers. With the ready workshop, close the dialog through Back, reach the link by keyboard and modeled controller, and verify activation neither applies the draft nor writes player progress. Keep modal and practice input ownership intact. Check target size, focus visibility and actual navigation in portrait/short landscape separately from DOM tests.”
